# Component Architecture

All React components must follow a modular folder structure.

## Folder Structure

```
ComponentName/
├── index.ts           # Re-exports only
├── ComponentName.tsx  # Component logic
├── ComponentName.style.ts  # Styled components
└── ComponentName.types.ts  # Types and interfaces (if needed)
```

## Rules

### 1. One Responsibility Per File
- `*.tsx` — Component logic only
- `*.style.ts` — Styled components only
- `*.types.ts` — Types and interfaces only
- `index.ts` — Re-exports only

### 2. Index File Pattern
The `index.ts` must only re-export, never contain logic:

```ts
export * from './ComponentName';
export * from './ComponentName.types';
```

### 3. Import Pattern
Always import from the folder barrel via **relative paths** (not deep file paths):

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
import { Button } from '../../components/Button';

// ❌ BAD
import { Button } from '../../components/Button/Button';
```

Do **not** use the `@/` alias in new code — see `import-sections.mdc`.

### 4. Named Exports Only
Always use named exports, never default exports:

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
export const Button: React.FC<ButtonProps> = () => { ... };

// ❌ BAD
export default Button;
```

## Example Structure

```ts
// Button/index.ts
export * from './Button';
export * from './Button.types';

// Button/Button.types.ts
export type ButtonVariant = 'primary' | 'secondary';
export interface ButtonProps { ... }

// Button/Button.style.ts
export const StyledButton = styled.button`...`;

// Button/Button.tsx
import { ButtonProps } from './Button.types';
import { StyledButton } from './Button.style';

export const Button: React.FC<ButtonProps> = ({ ... }) => { ... };
```
